  _citation_special_details
         primary   
;
  The Certification of Standard Reference Material 1979: 
  Powder Diffraction Line Profile Standard for Crystallite Size Analysis
;        'J. Res. NIST'      2020      10.6028/jres.125.020          
; Primary paper on this SRM, 
  describing data collection and analysis using Fundamental Parameters Approach
  and Bruker AXS Topas software.

Attached measured data are exactly the raw data sets used for certification. 

However, the fits have been recomputed for the purposes of this data release. 
The instrument parameters have been re-refined, and
the calculated results field contain a pattern calculated from these new parameters.

There are three data sets in here.  
The first is the measured data directly as returned from 11-bm. 
The second has had its angular scale adjusted based on a cubic angular fit to a high-resolution scan of SRM660c material.  
The third is the fit to the data set, based on  Rietveld analysis carried out in Topas, also with corrected angles.

Note: Certain commercial equipment, instruments, software, or materials are identified in this file 
in order to specify the experimental procedure adequately. Such identification is not intended to imply r
ecommendation or endorsement by the U.S. government, nor is it intended to imply that the 
materials or equipment identified are necessarily the best available for the purpose.
;        
         certificate         
; Standard Reference Material 1979: Line shape standard for nanocrystals 
  (Zinc Oxide powder)
;        https://www-s.nist.gov/srmors/view_detail.cfm?srm=1979      2020      .        'Current official certificate for this SRM'      
         11bm-1    'A twelve-analyzer detector system for high-resolution powder diffraction'     'J. Synch. Rad.'   2008     10.1107/S0909049508018438    .        
         11bm-2    
;
A dedicated powder diffraction beamline at the Advanced Photon Source: 
Commissioning and early operational results
;        'Rev. Sci. Instr.'  2008      10.1063/1.2969260   .         
         11bm-3    
;
Management of metadata and automation for mail-in measurements 
with the APS 11-BM high-throughput, 
high-resolution synchrotron powder diffractometer
;        'J. Appl. Cryst.'   2009      10.1107/S0021889809035717     .         
         funding   
;
Use of the Advanced Photon Source (APS) at Argonne National Laboratory 
was supported by the U.S. Department of Energy, Office of Science, Office of Basic Energy Sciences, 
under Contract No. DE-AC02-06CH11357
;        .         .         .         . 
